"text": " This free kick bent so much, a ball boy ducked, and the goalkeeper didn't even move. June 3rd, 1997. Lyon, France. Brazil against France. 21 minutes. A free kick almost 40 yards from goal. Roberto Carlos walks back 18 steps. He runs in and hits it with the outside of his left foot. The ball flies past the wall so wide that a ball boy way off to the right ducks. Then it swerves back towards the goal, off the post and in. The goalkeeper, Fabien Barthez, never moved. For years, people called it a fluke. In 2010, French physicists explained it. Hit hard enough, from far enough, a spinning ball curls more and more in a spiral. So luck or physics? Tell me in the comments.",
